  "id": "be48444f-6092-5ee6-8b34-42dc76538101",
  "slug": "bakers-secret-pie-crust",
  "name": "Baker's Secret Pie Crust",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "Your next pie can be a winner at home with this award-winning recipe for pie crust. Just follow this reliable recipe that calls for both cake and all-purpose flours along with other familiar crust ingredients, some pulsing with an electric food processor, and a few quick chillings in the freezer.",
  "cuisine": null,
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Measure butter & shortening onto a plate, put into freezer for about 20 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Measure cake flour, all-purpose flour, sugar, salt and baking powder into the bowl of a food processor. Pulse for a few seconds to mix."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Take 1/2 of the cold butter and 1/2 of the cold shortening, put into processor with dry ingredients and pulse off and on for about 1 minute. Scrape down twice while doing this."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Take remainder of the cold butter & cold shortening and cut in very briefly with the processor, leaving visible pea-sized chunks. Do not over process at this stage!"
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "In a measuring cup, mix egg yolk and vinegar together, add ice cubes and water. Let this get chilled, about 3 to 4 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Remove mixed flours and shortening from processor, put into a large mixing bowl. Sprinkle approximately 4 to 5 tablespoons of this egg, water, vinegar mixture, a little at a time, mixing gently with a fork. The key to this is, you do not want a wet dough, and you do not want to overmix."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Place this dough into plastic wrap or plastic bag, chill in refrigerator for a few minutes. (May also be frozen for a few weeks at this stage for future use)."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Remove from refrigerator and roll out. This makes absolutely the BEST pie crusts. I have won County Fair competitions with this pie crust. Double for making a 2-crust pie."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
